# J23 — Evidence loop: recommend-then-authorize scan + real findings
# (harness fixture target).
#
# Runs against the HARNESS-OWNED fixture repo (@TMP_TARGET), never an
# operator checkout: the journey needs deterministic clean state, and the
# master contract forbids deleting `.kuzushi` under an operator-designated
# target. Real-monorepo coverage lives in J25–J27. Drives the guided
# Map-first lifecycle, captures the threat-model/recommender seeding state
# of the Scan configure card, then produces real findings with the
# deterministic built-in scanner and audits Review → Prove → Trace on a
# genuine finding (the fixture carries a real secret-scan hit).
#
# Known remaining baseline defects this journey evidences (expected FAIL rows
# until the matching kuzushi slices land):
#   - module-recommender launch is blocked on this target class ("Workspace
#     policy verification changed during its first attempt"), so the Scan
#     configure card degrades to generic defaults instead of a seeded plan;
#   - semgrep:scan passes an absolute scanning root, which semgrep >= 1.x
#     rejects ("Invalid scanning root") on every target.
# Fixed by Phase B slices (now expected PASS): phantom-invalidation
# rev:unknown wedge (slice 1); PARTIAL Map hand-off "Use map & choose Scan
# modules" + page digits under an unresolved result (slice 2).
name: Evidence loop scan + findings (fixture target)
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
shell: rm -rf "@TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi" && git -C "@TMP_TARGET" add -A >/dev/null 2>&1; git -C "@TMP_TARGET" -c user.email=devex@kuzushi -c user.name=kz-devex commit -qm fixture >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 KUZUSHI
# submit: self-normalizes to a clean Prompt by polling the footer mode
# markers, so no fixed settle delay is needed after the header appears.
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
wait: 2
# threat-model:build is model-backed by default and refuses on this modelless
# box; opt the Map plan's threat-model task into the runtime-free
# deterministic fold explicitly (session-scoped — never a silent fallback).
submit: options threat-model:build
wait: 1
submit: set pipeline deterministic
wait: 1
submit: scan
wait-for: 15 MAP · ROUTE
snap: map-route
expect: Map establishes the target context Scan engines will consume.
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 MAP · MODULES
# STRIDE needs a configured model; keep the workload run runtime-free.
keys: 4
wait: 1
keys: Enter
# Fresh workload target: repository context is missing, so the guided flow
# inserts the context prerequisite question and renumbers to 4 steps.
wait-for: 10 PREREQUISITE · STEP 3 OF 4
snap: map-context-prereq
expect: Build context
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 STEP 4 OF 4
keys: a
wait-live-snap: 300 RESULT READY | map-result-ready
# A healthy partial map is selectable AND continuable: the card offers the
# explicit "Use map & choose Scan modules" hand-off as row 3 (`Enter` takes
# the recommended action, which for partial evidence is plain "Use map").
expect: Use map & choose Scan modules
keys: 3
wait-live-snap: 20 SCAN · MODULES | configure-scan
# Desired: a seeded plan with rationales tied to recorded evidence. Baseline:
# the recommender is blocked on this target class, so this fails honestly.
expect: Lineage target rev:
expect: seeded by the threat model
expect: RECOMMENDED
ask: Configure — is the Scan plan seeded from recorded evidence (threat model / recommender) with per-row rationales, or does it degrade to a blind generic list on this target?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
# Deterministic real findings: the built-in secret scanner runs offline, $0.
submit: run secret-scan:scan {}
wait-for: 120 run receipt
wait: 2
# The RESULT checkpoint is not a modal: page digits keep navigating under an
# unresolved result (baseline G4 wedge, fixed by the fingerprint of slice 2).
nav-mode:
keys: 3
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Review | page-key-after-partial-result
ask: Result strip — can the operator resolve a PARTIAL result and keep using page keys, or is workbench navigation wedged until they know the findings verb?
submit: findings
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Review | review-real-findings
expect: FINDINGS
expect: SELECTED FINDING
expect: candidate
ask: Review — do real workload findings land in the queue with an honest proof ladder (candidate, unverified) and one selected identity with a clear next action?
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Prove | prove-real-finding
expect: PROOF SUBJECT · finding
expect: STATUS / NEXT
ask: Prove — is the proof subject labeled with the finding identity and does NEXT recommend evidence collection before patching?
keys: v
wait-live-snap: 10 INVESTIGATE · Enter draft command | investigation-card
expect: EVIDENCE GOALS
expect: SAFETY BOUNDARY
expect: STOP CONDITIONS
expect: nothing runs until you submit the drafted command
keys: v
wait: 1
keys: t
wait-live-snap: 10 TRACE · Enter draft trace:expand | trace-real-finding
expect: RECORDED PATH
expect: EXPANDED PATH · requested by operator
ask: Trace — on a real workload finding, is the recorded evidence path distinguished from operator-requested expansion without fabricating hops?
keys: t
wait: 1
# Chains are durable artifacts over corroborated findings: corroborate the
# real selected finding, fold + persist (findings:chains writes
# .kuzushi/v3/reports/chains.json + the scene snapshot), and audit the
# honest artifact state — this module's confirmed set composes no
# entry→impact pair, and the screen must say exactly that instead of
# fabricating a scenario.
nav-mode:
keys: 3
wait: 1
submit: decision confirmed corroborated in the evidence-loop chain audit
wait: 1
submit: run findings:chains {}
wait-for: 60 candidate chain(s)
wait: 1
# Resolve the chains-run checkpoint first (`u` commits the decisions); the
# collapsed RESULT surface otherwise owns the screen.
nav-mode:
keys: u
wait: 1
keys: C
wait-live-snap: 10 ATTACK CHAINS | chains-artifact
expect: confirmed finding(s) compose no entry→impact pair
expect: chains compose over CONFIRMED findings
keys: C
wait: 1
keys: Escape
